{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-715", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/715", "wordCount": 3938, "segments": [{"start": 15.0, "text": "Hi. Welcome to Core NFC"}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "Enhancements."}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "I hope everyone's had a great"}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "WWDC this year."}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "And I hope everyone had a great"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "time at the bash yesterday."}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "My name is Gordon."}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "I'm a member of the NFC Software"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "team here at Apple."}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "A little bit later, we'll bring"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "up another team member,"}, {"start": 28.0, "text": "Lawrence."}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "But let's talk NFC."}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "So two years ago, we introduced"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "the Core NFC framework to enable"}, {"start": 37.0, "text": "NDEF Tag reading within your"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "applications."}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "And last year, we introduced"}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "background tag scanning to"}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "support the automatic discovery"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "of NDEF Tags and application"}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "launching."}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "Now, however, since -- ever"}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "since we've launched the Core"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "NFC Framework, developers have"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "been asking for one specific"}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "thing. And here at Apple, we've"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "listened to your requests."}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "And this year, we are super"}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "excited to announce support for"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "both NDEF Tag writing and native"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "tag access."}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "So yep, thank you."}, {"start": 68.0, "text": "So not only will your applications be able to read and"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "write NDEF-formatted tags, but"}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "you'll be able to interact with"}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "tags using their native"}, {"start": 74.0, "text": "protocols."}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "And this has a huge impact on"}, {"start": 77.0, "text": "the kinds of things you can do"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "with NFC within your"}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "applications."}, {"start": 80.0, "text": "For example, you can read"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "passports, contact with smart"}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "cards, and interact with"}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "NFC-enabled hardware."}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "And all this is available on"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "iPhone 7 and later phones."}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "So after we review the API"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "changes, we'll take a look at"}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "how to write an NDEF tag within"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "your applications."}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "Then we'll dive into using"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "native tag access."}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "And finally, end up with a demo"}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "showing all of this in action."}, {"start": 109.0, "text": "So let's take a look at the new"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "API changes."}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "As a quick review, the general"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "structure of the Core NFC"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "Framework remains the same as it"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "does today. Your applications will retrieve"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "a reader session object from the"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "Framework."}, {"start": 123.0, "text": "And when that session becomes"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "active, you're free to go ahead"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "and perform NFC operations."}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "The tag-reading action sheet"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "will still be shown on-screen"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "anytime a reader session is"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "active."}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "And the new tag writing and"}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "native tag access features are"}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "available to your applications."}, {"start": 142.0, "text": "However, the background tag"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "scanning feature still requires"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "NDEF formatted tags and is"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "read-only."}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "Also, the existing 60-second"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "maximum scan time still exists"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "for each reader session."}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "So what is new?"}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "So this year, there's a new NFC"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "tag-reader session which will"}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "allow your applications to scan"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "for and connect to tags based on"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "their underlying technologies."}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "It will also allow you to stop"}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "and restart the polling cycle to"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "discover new tags or to"}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "reconnect if needed."}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "Also, the NFCNDEFReaderSession"}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "has been modified to also"}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "support tag writing."}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "Now, both of these sessions will"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "provide your applications with"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "NFC tag objects, allowing you to"}, {"start": 188.0, "text": "use a new tag-based interface"}, {"start": 190.0, "text": "when interacting with tags."}, {"start": 194.0, "text": "So here's a quick look at the"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "new tag protocols in Core NFC."}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "As you can see, there are"}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "protocols for all the major"}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "types."}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "NDEF, ISO7816, MIFARE, ISO15693,"}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "and FeliCa. Now, if you're not familiar with"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "all the various NFC"}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "technologies, I would suggest"}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "focusing first on NDEF."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "So let's go over the basic steps of how to use these new features"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "in Core NFC."}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "First, you'll need to enable the"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "entitlement in Xcode, just as"}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "you do today."}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "So here's an example of an"}, {"start": 226.0, "text": "application enabling the NFC"}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "capabilities."}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "There are no special permissions"}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "required to do this."}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "And as you can see here, there"}, {"start": 234.0, "text": "are two different capabilities,"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "one for NDEF, and one for native"}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "tag access."}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "So next, you'll need to decide"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "what your application requires,"}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "NDEF or native access, and use"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "the appropriate reader session."}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "You'll need to implement the new"}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "protocol delegate callbacks to"}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "receive the new tag objects."}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "Once you have the tag object,"}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "you use the reader session to go"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "ahead and connect to the tag."}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "At that point, you're free to go"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "ahead and perform all your"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "interactions using the tag"}, {"start": 266.0, "text": "object."}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "And finally, when you're done,"}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "invalidate the session and"}, {"start": 273.0, "text": "release your tag."}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "All right. So as I mentioned, if you're new"}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "to NFC, start first with the NFC"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "Data Exchange Format, or NDEF."}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "It is the easiest way to add NFC"}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "capabilities to your"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "applications."}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "The new tag running support"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "allows for quick implementation"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "and prototyping using any --"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "NDEF-formatted tag regardless of"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "its type. As an example, an NDEF tag can"}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "be used in the same manner as a"}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "QR code and can easily be"}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "integrated into many existing"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "use cases."}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "To extend that even further,"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "using the new tag-writing"}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "support in NFC, you can create"}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "NFC tags that are compatible"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "with background tag scanning"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "directly from iOS."}, {"start": 313.0, "text": "So let's take a look."}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "Yeah. Thank you."}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "Let's take a closer look at just"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "how simple it is to write an"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "NDEF tag within your"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "application."}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "So as I noted, you'll need to"}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "use the NFCNDEFReaderSession for"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "this."}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "And you'll need to implement the"}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "new didDetect tags callback"}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "method to receive the NDEF tag"}, {"start": 332.0, "text": "objects."}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "This will allow your application"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "to do various things, such as"}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "query the NDEF-related"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "information about the tag,"}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "including its maximum capacity,"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "and determine whether the tag is"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "writeable or not."}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "You'll be able to read the NDEF"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "message, write the NDEF message."}, {"start": 349.0, "text": "And if the tag supports it, even"}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "lock the tag so that it can no"}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "longer be rewritten."}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "So let's take a look at some"}, {"start": 355.0, "text": "code."}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "To start writing an NDEF tag, we"}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "instantiate our"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "NFCNDEFReaderSession."}, {"start": 361.0, "text": "We provided our new delegate."}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "And we set the"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "invalidateAfterFirstRead"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "parameter to false."}, {"start": 372.0, "text": "Next, when a tag is discovered,"}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "we receive it in our new"}, {"start": 374.0, "text": "Delegate callback method here."}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "Once we have a tag, we then send"}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "it to the reader session's"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "Connect method to go ahead and"}, {"start": 383.0, "text": "connect to the tag."}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "Now at this point, your tag will"}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "remain connected until you"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "either connect to a different"}, {"start": 388.0, "text": "tag, restart polling, or"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "invalidate your session."}, {"start": 397.0, "text": "So the next step here, after we've connected to the tag, we"}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "go ahead and query the NDEF"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "information."}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "If the tag returns a read-write"}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "status, then we're free to go"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "ahead and write a new message to"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "the tag."}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "So the next step here."}, {"start": 411.0, "text": "We create an NFC NDEF message"}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "with our payload and then send"}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "it to the tag's writeNDEF method"}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "to update the tag."}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "Finally, when we're all done, we"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "call the invalidate method."}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "This will terminate all NFC"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "operations and end our session."}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "And that's it."}, {"start": 430.0, "text": "Pretty simple, right? This is all it takes to write an"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "NDEF tag within your app."}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "Now there might be some use"}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "cases where you need to interact"}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "with tags that are not NDEF"}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "formatted. And for that, we'll need to go"}, {"start": 439.0, "text": "ahead and use native tag access."}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "So let's dive into that."}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "We'll start first with ISO7816."}, {"start": 450.0, "text": "The ISO7816 interface is used in"}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "Type A and Type B NFC tags."}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "And it's used in a variety of"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "different use cases, including"}, {"start": 459.0, "text": "electronic IDs such as"}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "passports, access, contact with"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "smart cards, payments, and"}, {"start": 466.0, "text": "transit systems."}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "Tags that support 7816 utilize"}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "the Application Protocol Data"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "Unit interface."}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "This is commonly referred to as"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "APDU."}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "And your applications will be"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "able to send and receive APDU"}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "commands using the 7816 tag"}, {"start": 480.0, "text": "objects."}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "Now there are a few special requirements for interacting"}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "with 7816 tags."}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "So let's go over those first before we look at some code."}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "First, your application will"}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "need to add an entry into its"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "info.plist file that declares"}, {"start": 498.0, "text": "the specific application"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "identifiers, or AIDs, which your"}, {"start": 501.0, "text": "application intends to use."}, {"start": 507.0, "text": "Next, once Core NFC has discovered a tag, it will first"}, {"start": 509.0, "text": "check to see if that tag"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "supports an AID listed in your"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "application's info.plist file."}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "It does this by trying to select"}, {"start": 516.0, "text": "each AID in turn until it finds"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "a match."}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "At that point, the Delegate"}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "callback will be invoked, and"}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "you will receive the tag object"}, {"start": 524.0, "text": "with that AID preselected."}, {"start": 526.0, "text": "However, at this point, you're"}, {"start": 528.0, "text": "free to go ahead and select any"}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "other AID listed in your"}, {"start": 530.0, "text": "info.plist file."}, {"start": 539.0, "text": "Now, we're excited about these new features in Core NFC."}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "However, for the time being,"}, {"start": 542.0, "text": "reading payment cards will not"}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "be supported."}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "So here's an example of an"}, {"start": 548.0, "text": "application info.plist file"}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "listing the AIDs it intends to use."}, {"start": 554.0, "text": "Here, you can see the application is listing the AID"}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "for NDEF operations."}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "So now, we'll take a look at the actual 7816 tag object."}, {"start": 567.0, "text": "The protocol has properties that"}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "are specific to the 7816"}, {"start": 571.0, "text": "technology."}, {"start": 572.0, "text": "You can see the attributes here"}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "include the unique identifier"}, {"start": 575.0, "text": "and the historical bytes."}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "So is anyone excited about the"}, {"start": 578.0, "text": "unique ID here?"}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "This is the second-most popular"}, {"start": 581.0, "text": "request that we get."}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "There's also a sendCommand"}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "method for transmitting any form"}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "of APDU to the tag and receiving"}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "the response."}, {"start": 592.0, "text": "So to start scanning the 7816"}, {"start": 594.0, "text": "tags, as I mentioned, the first"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "thing that we'll need to do is"}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "implement a Delegate object"}, {"start": 598.0, "text": "which conforms to the"}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "NFCTagReaderSession Delegate"}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "protocol."}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "There are only three required"}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "methods, and you can see them up"}, {"start": 603.0, "text": "here."}, {"start": 609.0, "text": "So to start scanning for 7816"}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "tags, we instantiate our"}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "NFCTagReaderSession object,"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "provide it our delegate, and set"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "the polling option to ISO14443."}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "This is the underlying NFC"}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "technology for Type A and Type B"}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "tags."}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "Next, when Core NFC discovers a"}, {"start": 629.0, "text": "tag that has a matching AID, we"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "receive it in our Delegate"}, {"start": 631.0, "text": "callback."}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "And once we're assured that we"}, {"start": 637.0, "text": "have a 7816 tag, we use the"}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "reader's session.connect method"}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "to go ahead and connect to the tag."}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "And finally, after we're"}, {"start": 647.0, "text": "connected, we create an APDU"}, {"start": 649.0, "text": "using the helper class and use"}, {"start": 651.0, "text": "the same command method of the"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "tag to transmit the APDU and"}, {"start": 653.0, "text": "receive its response."}, {"start": 658.0, "text": "Now during the transaction, we"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "may find an application-related"}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "error has occurred, and we"}, {"start": 662.0, "text": "should not continue."}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "As an example, imagine we're"}, {"start": 665.0, "text": "trying to read a passport."}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "And it turns out we don't have"}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "the proper credentials, or we've"}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "calculated the password"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "incorrectly. In a scenario like this, we"}, {"start": 673.0, "text": "would really like to indicate"}, {"start": 674.0, "text": "this error to the user."}, {"start": 676.0, "text": "Calling the Invalidate method"}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "with an error message will"}, {"start": 679.0, "text": "invalidate the session, and an"}, {"start": 681.0, "text": "error symbol, along with the"}, {"start": 682.0, "text": "supplied error message, will be"}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "shown on the action sheet UI"}, {"start": 685.0, "text": "rather than a checkmark."}, {"start": 690.0, "text": "So here's an example of what this error indication looks"}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "like."}, {"start": 692.0, "text": "We'll see this later in the"}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "demo."}, {"start": 694.0, "text": "But this is pretty great, right?"}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "This is the third-most requested"}, {"start": 696.0, "text": "feature we get."}, {"start": 704.0, "text": "And just for reference, here's the existing success indication."}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "So that was 7816."}, {"start": 712.0, "text": "Let's move on to our second"}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "technology, MIFARE."}, {"start": 714.0, "text": "MIFARE is the technology similar"}, {"start": 716.0, "text": "to 7816."}, {"start": 717.0, "text": "And it's based on NFC Type A"}, {"start": 718.0, "text": "tags."}, {"start": 720.0, "text": "MIFARE is a technology defined"}, {"start": 721.0, "text": "by NXP and is used heavily in"}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "ticketing and badging systems"}, {"start": 724.0, "text": "throughout the world."}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "So the NFC MIFARE tag protocol"}, {"start": 731.0, "text": "has properties similar to that"}, {"start": 732.0, "text": "of 7816."}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "In addition, there's another"}, {"start": 735.0, "text": "property of the MIFARE family."}, {"start": 737.0, "text": "This will indicate the specific"}, {"start": 738.0, "text": "MIFARE tag type that has been"}, {"start": 740.0, "text": "discovered."}, {"start": 741.0, "text": "It can be MIFARE Ultralight,"}, {"start": 742.0, "text": "MIFARE Plus, or DESFire."}, {"start": 744.0, "text": "At this time, MIFARE Classic"}, {"start": 746.0, "text": "tags are not supported."}, {"start": 748.0, "text": "There's also a method here for"}, {"start": 750.0, "text": "sending any MIFARE command."}, {"start": 752.0, "text": "In addition, there's a"}, {"start": 753.0, "text": "convenience method for sending"}, {"start": 754.0, "text": "7816 APDUs for those tags, such"}, {"start": 757.0, "text": "as DESFire and Plus, which will"}, {"start": 758.0, "text": "support them."}, {"start": 762.0, "text": "So now, let's see this in action."}, {"start": 765.0, "text": "Just start scanning for a MIFARE"}, {"start": 766.0, "text": "tag."}, {"start": 767.0, "text": "We again instantiate our tag"}, {"start": 768.0, "text": "reader session."}, {"start": 769.0, "text": "Again, we set our polling option"}, {"start": 771.0, "text": "to ISO14443."}, {"start": 772.0, "text": "And we set the Delegate and Call"}, {"start": 775.0, "text": "Begin."}, {"start": 779.0, "text": "Please note that a MIFARE tag"}, {"start": 780.0, "text": "that supports a 7816 interface"}, {"start": 783.0, "text": "and contains an AID listing the"}, {"start": 784.0, "text": "applications info.plist file"}, {"start": 786.0, "text": "will instead be returned as a"}, {"start": 787.0, "text": "7816 object and not a MIFARE"}, {"start": 790.0, "text": "object."}, {"start": 794.0, "text": "So at this point, when our callback gets invoked, we"}, {"start": 795.0, "text": "specifically check to make sure"}, {"start": 796.0, "text": "that we have a MIFARE tag object"}, {"start": 797.0, "text": "returned."}, {"start": 802.0, "text": "Once we're sure we have one, we"}, {"start": 803.0, "text": "send it to the reader's"}, {"start": 804.0, "text": "session.connect method and"}, {"start": 805.0, "text": "connect to the tag."}, {"start": 806.0, "text": "And then use the tag to send a"}, {"start": 810.0, "text": "MIFARE command."}, {"start": 816.0, "text": "Okay, so that's two of the four"}, {"start": 817.0, "text": "technologies."}, {"start": 818.0, "text": "So let's look at ISO15693."}, {"start": 819.0, "text": "This is also known as type five"}, {"start": 823.0, "text": "or vicinity tags."}, {"start": 824.0, "text": "And these are commonly used in"}, {"start": 825.0, "text": "retail, industrial, and even"}, {"start": 826.0, "text": "medical applications."}, {"start": 831.0, "text": "So once again, this protocol has"}, {"start": 832.0, "text": "properties specific to the"}, {"start": 834.0, "text": "ISO15693 technology."}, {"start": 836.0, "text": "Here, we also have the unique"}, {"start": 837.0, "text": "identifier, as well as the"}, {"start": 839.0, "text": "manufacture code and the serial"}, {"start": 840.0, "text": "number."}, {"start": 846.0, "text": "And the command set for 15693,"}, {"start": 848.0, "text": "if you have not seen it, is"}, {"start": 849.0, "text": "quite large."}, {"start": 850.0, "text": "And the protocol has convenience"}, {"start": 851.0, "text": "methods for some of the common"}, {"start": 852.0, "text": "operations."}, {"start": 853.0, "text": "You can see them listed up here."}, {"start": 855.0, "text": "They cover reading and writing"}, {"start": 857.0, "text": "single or multiple blocks,"}, {"start": 859.0, "text": "locking blocks, select, and"}, {"start": 861.0, "text": "reset."}, {"start": 863.0, "text": "Again, there's also a method for"}, {"start": 864.0, "text": "sending any custom command."}, {"start": 866.0, "text": "You can construct any command"}, {"start": 867.0, "text": "according to the ISO15693"}, {"start": 869.0, "text": "specification and use that"}, {"start": 871.0, "text": "method to send it."}, {"start": 873.0, "text": "You can go ahead and refer to"}, {"start": 874.0, "text": "the specification for more"}, {"start": 875.0, "text": "details."}, {"start": 880.0, "text": "So to start scanning for"}, {"start": 881.0, "text": "vicinity tags, which should now"}, {"start": 883.0, "text": "be looking very familiar to"}, {"start": 884.0, "text": "everyone, we create our"}, {"start": 886.0, "text": "NFCTagReaderSession, provide it"}, {"start": 888.0, "text": "our delegate."}, {"start": 889.0, "text": "But this time, we changed the"}, {"start": 891.0, "text": "polling option to ISO15693."}, {"start": 898.0, "text": "When Core NFC discovers a 15693"}, {"start": 900.0, "text": "tag, again, we receive the tag"}, {"start": 901.0, "text": "in our callback."}, {"start": 906.0, "text": "We again verify that we have the"}, {"start": 907.0, "text": "proper tag type and then connect"}, {"start": 908.0, "text": "to it using the sessions.connect"}, {"start": 909.0, "text": "method."}, {"start": 914.0, "text": "And once connected, we use the"}, {"start": 915.0, "text": "tag to issue a readSingleBlock"}, {"start": 916.0, "text": "command."}, {"start": 923.0, "text": "So finally, we're on to our fourth and final technology,"}, {"start": 925.0, "text": "FeliCa."}, {"start": 926.0, "text": "FeliCa is a format defined by"}, {"start": 927.0, "text": "Sony, and it's used heavily in"}, {"start": 928.0, "text": "transit and payment systems"}, {"start": 929.0, "text": "around Japan."}, {"start": 933.0, "text": "Now the FeliCa usage also has"}, {"start": 935.0, "text": "some additional requirements."}, {"start": 937.0, "text": "Similar to 7816, your"}, {"start": 940.0, "text": "application will need to add an"}, {"start": 941.0, "text": "entry into the info.plist file"}, {"start": 944.0, "text": "that declares the specific"}, {"start": 945.0, "text": "FeliCa system codes your"}, {"start": 946.0, "text": "application intends to use."}, {"start": 948.0, "text": "And for security and privacy"}, {"start": 949.0, "text": "reasons, we're asking that these"}, {"start": 951.0, "text": "be discreet FeliCa system codes"}, {"start": 952.0, "text": "and not wildcard entries."}, {"start": 957.0, "text": "Again, similar to 7816, when"}, {"start": 959.0, "text": "Core NFC discovers a FeliCa tag,"}, {"start": 961.0, "text": "we'll first validate -- detect"}, {"start": 962.0, "text": "that that tag contains a system"}, {"start": 964.0, "text": "code listed in your info.plist"}, {"start": 966.0, "text": "file."}, {"start": 967.0, "text": "If it does, you'll receive the"}, {"start": 968.0, "text": "tag and the Delegate callback."}, {"start": 969.0, "text": "If it does not, the callback"}, {"start": 971.0, "text": "does not get invoked, and your"}, {"start": 972.0, "text": "application does not get"}, {"start": 973.0, "text": "notified about the presence of"}, {"start": 974.0, "text": "the tag."}, {"start": 978.0, "text": "So here's an example of an"}, {"start": 979.0, "text": "info.plist file registering for"}, {"start": 981.0, "text": "FeliCa system code reserved for"}, {"start": 984.0, "text": "NDEF operations."}, {"start": 992.0, "text": "Again, taking a look at the"}, {"start": 993.0, "text": "FeliCa tag protocol here, we see"}, {"start": 995.0, "text": "properties specific to FeliCa."}, {"start": 997.0, "text": "We have the manufacturer ID, or"}, {"start": 998.0, "text": "IDM, and the current selected"}, {"start": 1000.0, "text": "system code."}, {"start": 1002.0, "text": "Also, there's a sendFeliCaCommand method for"}, {"start": 1004.0, "text": "sending any FeliCa command to"}, {"start": 1005.0, "text": "the tag."}, {"start": 1009.0, "text": "And this protocol also has convenience methods for some of"}, {"start": 1011.0, "text": "the common FeliCa operations."}, {"start": 1012.0, "text": "You can go ahead and refer to"}, {"start": 1015.0, "text": "Sony's FeliCa command"}, {"start": 1016.0, "text": "specification for more details."}, {"start": 1021.0, "text": "So continuing what should now be"}, {"start": 1022.0, "text": "a very familiar usage model, we"}, {"start": 1025.0, "text": "instantiated an NFCTagReaderSession, provide it"}, {"start": 1027.0, "text": "our delegate, and this time,"}, {"start": 1029.0, "text": "changed the polling option to"}, {"start": 1030.0, "text": "ISO18092, which is the NFC"}, {"start": 1032.0, "text": "technology for FeliCa."}, {"start": 1038.0, "text": "So once Core NFC has discovered"}, {"start": 1039.0, "text": "a tag and found a matching"}, {"start": 1040.0, "text": "system code, we again receive"}, {"start": 1041.0, "text": "the tag object in our same"}, {"start": 1042.0, "text": "delegate."}, {"start": 1045.0, "text": "We ensure that we have the"}, {"start": 1046.0, "text": "proper tag type we were"}, {"start": 1047.0, "text": "expecting and then connect to"}, {"start": 1048.0, "text": "the tag."}, {"start": 1054.0, "text": "And then finally, we use the tag"}, {"start": 1056.0, "text": "to send a requestResponse"}, {"start": 1057.0, "text": "command."}, {"start": 1058.0, "text": "So we've now covered NDEF tag"}, {"start": 1059.0, "text": "writing and interacting with"}, {"start": 1061.0, "text": "tags using all four of the"}, {"start": 1062.0, "text": "native technologies."}, {"start": 1066.0, "text": "So at this point, I'm going to"}, {"start": 1067.0, "text": "bring Lawrence onstage and show"}, {"start": 1068.0, "text": "us a demo of all of this in"}, {"start": 1069.0, "text": "action."}, {"start": 1077.0, "text": "All right, thank you, Gordon."}, {"start": 1079.0, "text": "Hello, everyone."}, {"start": 1081.0, "text": "Welcome."}, {"start": 1084.0, "text": "To demonstrate how Core NFC"}, {"start": 1086.0, "text": "Framework can be used in a"}, {"start": 1087.0, "text": "real-life example, let me take"}, {"start": 1090.0, "text": "you through a quick journey of"}, {"start": 1092.0, "text": "my imaginary fishmonger."}, {"start": 1096.0, "text": "As a tech savvy fishmonger, I"}, {"start": 1098.0, "text": "have heard that the NFC"}, {"start": 1100.0, "text": "technologies can improve"}, {"start": 1102.0, "text": "customer engagement and also be"}, {"start": 1104.0, "text": "used in inventory management."}, {"start": 1107.0, "text": "After listening on this great"}, {"start": 1108.0, "text": "presentation, I have decided to"}, {"start": 1111.0, "text": "create two applications to help"}, {"start": 1113.0, "text": "my business, The Great Fish"}, {"start": 1115.0, "text": "Company."}, {"start": 1118.0, "text": "I'm going to use NFC in two"}, {"start": 1119.0, "text": "ways."}, {"start": 1121.0, "text": "First, I'm going to create NFC"}, {"start": 1124.0, "text": "NDEF tags to describe my"}, {"start": 1125.0, "text": "product."}, {"start": 1127.0, "text": "And second, I'm going to create"}, {"start": 1128.0, "text": "coupon tags using MIFARE"}, {"start": 1130.0, "text": "Ultralight tags, which is also"}, {"start": 1132.0, "text": "known as NFC Type II tags."}, {"start": 1141.0, "text": "Here is an overview of how we"}, {"start": 1142.0, "text": "deliver our products."}, {"start": 1144.0, "text": "After we catch our fish, we"}, {"start": 1146.0, "text": "integrate NFC NDEF tag to"}, {"start": 1150.0, "text": "describe the catch."}, {"start": 1152.0, "text": "The message contains the fish"}, {"start": 1154.0, "text": "they have catch, the fish name,"}, {"start": 1156.0, "text": "and the price."}, {"start": 1158.0, "text": "The tag is then attached to the"}, {"start": 1160.0, "text": "product packaging and eventually"}, {"start": 1161.0, "text": "gets delivered to our customers."}, {"start": 1164.0, "text": "The first application that I'm"}, {"start": 1165.0, "text": "going to create is called the"}, {"start": 1166.0, "text": "Fish Tag Creator."}, {"start": 1168.0, "text": "This is what it looks like here."}, {"start": 1173.0, "text": "Once I've entered all the information into my app, I can"}, {"start": 1176.0, "text": "click on the Write to Tag button"}, {"start": 1178.0, "text": "to write to the NDEF tag."}, {"start": 1181.0, "text": "The Fish Tag Creator application"}, {"start": 1182.0, "text": "also allows me to create NFC"}, {"start": 1185.0, "text": "coupon codes to promote my"}, {"start": 1188.0, "text": "business."}, {"start": 1189.0, "text": "I use a MIFARE Ultralight tag to"}, {"start": 1191.0, "text": "store the special coupon code"}, {"start": 1192.0, "text": "and send it to my customers."}, {"start": 1194.0, "text": "Here, I can select one of the"}, {"start": 1197.0, "text": "three possible coupon values to"}, {"start": 1199.0, "text": "write."}, {"start": 1200.0, "text": "The second application that I"}, {"start": 1201.0, "text": "create is called a Fish Tag"}, {"start": 1203.0, "text": "Reader."}, {"start": 1205.0, "text": "My customer will be able to download this app from the App"}, {"start": 1207.0, "text": "Store to read the NDEF fish tag"}, {"start": 1209.0, "text": "that come with their purchase."}, {"start": 1212.0, "text": "In the first panel, we have the"}, {"start": 1215.0, "text": "Click Scan button to scan the"}, {"start": 1218.0, "text": "fish tag that comes with the"}, {"start": 1219.0, "text": "fish."}, {"start": 1220.0, "text": "The app would then display the"}, {"start": 1222.0, "text": "information stored it on the"}, {"start": 1223.0, "text": "tag."}, {"start": 1224.0, "text": "In the second panel, we can"}, {"start": 1226.0, "text": "click on the Scan Coupon button"}, {"start": 1228.0, "text": "to read our MIFARE Ultralight"}, {"start": 1229.0, "text": "fish tag -- coupon tags."}, {"start": 1232.0, "text": "Customer can redeem this coupon"}, {"start": 1233.0, "text": "in their future purchase."}, {"start": 1235.0, "text": "Now let's take a look at both of"}, {"start": 1237.0, "text": "these apps in actions."}, {"start": 1245.0, "text": "All right. I have basically put the -- the"}, {"start": 1248.0, "text": "Fish Tag Reader app right --"}, {"start": 1250.0, "text": "creator app right now."}, {"start": 1253.0, "text": "Today I brought with me a"}, {"start": 1256.0, "text": "creative rainbow salmon with me."}, {"start": 1262.0, "text": "Let me first select today's"}, {"start": 1263.0, "text": "dates and the fish name, which"}, {"start": 1265.0, "text": "is Creative Salmon."}, {"start": 1267.0, "text": "Okay, this one is definitely the"}, {"start": 1269.0, "text": "large size, right?"}, {"start": 1273.0, "text": "So now I click on the Write to"}, {"start": 1274.0, "text": "Tag button."}, {"start": 1276.0, "text": "The action sheet will be shown."}, {"start": 1278.0, "text": "And now, at this point, I can"}, {"start": 1279.0, "text": "hold my phone near the NDEF tag."}, {"start": 1285.0, "text": "Bingo."}, {"start": 1288.0, "text": "Now let me next then create a"}, {"start": 1290.0, "text": "coupon tag for your audience"}, {"start": 1291.0, "text": "here."}, {"start": 1292.0, "text": "I'm going to select Create"}, {"start": 1294.0, "text": "Coupon button."}, {"start": 1298.0, "text": "I'm going to choose a 50% off"}, {"start": 1299.0, "text": "since, you know, this is a"}, {"start": 1301.0, "text": "special WWDC promotion, right?"}, {"start": 1306.0, "text": "All right, so let's click on the"}, {"start": 1307.0, "text": "button."}, {"start": 1308.0, "text": "The action sheet again will be"}, {"start": 1309.0, "text": "shown on the screen."}, {"start": 1310.0, "text": "And now, I can hold my iPhone"}, {"start": 1312.0, "text": "near the coupon tag."}, {"start": 1316.0, "text": "Voila!"}, {"start": 1320.0, "text": "Okay, so now let's switch over"}, {"start": 1321.0, "text": "to the NFC Tag Readers app to"}, {"start": 1325.0, "text": "retest all my NFC tags."}, {"start": 1330.0, "text": "Here, I have the app open."}, {"start": 1332.0, "text": "I'm going to press on the Scan"}, {"start": 1333.0, "text": "Tag button and read my NDEF fish"}, {"start": 1335.0, "text": "tag."}, {"start": 1342.0, "text": "The description of the product"}, {"start": 1343.0, "text": "is now displayed on the screen."}, {"start": 1345.0, "text": "Wow, that's cool."}, {"start": 1347.0, "text": "Alright. Now let me try to scan"}, {"start": 1350.0, "text": "the coupon tag."}, {"start": 1352.0, "text": "This is done by selecting the"}, {"start": 1354.0, "text": "second panel and clicking on the"}, {"start": 1356.0, "text": "Scan Coupon button."}, {"start": 1364.0, "text": "All right, yeah."}, {"start": 1365.0, "text": "This is the fish 50% off coupon."}, {"start": 1368.0, "text": "Okay, so now let me try to read"}, {"start": 1370.0, "text": "the second coupon again."}, {"start": 1376.0, "text": "Okay, this is not a valid"}, {"start": 1377.0, "text": "coupon."}, {"start": 1378.0, "text": "So after seeing both of these"}, {"start": 1380.0, "text": "are running in actions, let me"}, {"start": 1382.0, "text": "switch over to the source code"}, {"start": 1384.0, "text": "and take a look at how this is implemented."}, {"start": 1392.0, "text": "All right, let's walk through the Fish Tag Creative Offers."}, {"start": 1401.0, "text": "Here, I'll set the NDEF and"}, {"start": 1402.0, "text": "native tag capabilities in my"}, {"start": 1405.0, "text": "entitlement file."}, {"start": 1406.0, "text": "This is because I'm going to use"}, {"start": 1408.0, "text": "both the NDEF and tag readings"}, {"start": 1410.0, "text": "-- reader session in my"}, {"start": 1411.0, "text": "application."}, {"start": 1418.0, "text": "Now let's take a look at the"}, {"start": 1420.0, "text": "Main View controller to see how"}, {"start": 1422.0, "text": "they NDEF writer is being"}, {"start": 1423.0, "text": "implemented."}, {"start": 1434.0, "text": "In the --"}, {"start": 1438.0, "text": "Sorry, one second here."}, {"start": 1444.0, "text": "In the Write Tag Action"}, {"start": 1445.0, "text": "function, we have to instantiate"}, {"start": 1447.0, "text": "an NFCNDEFReaderSession."}, {"start": 1450.0, "text": "We set the alert message and"}, {"start": 1453.0, "text": "call the Begin Method to start a"}, {"start": 1454.0, "text": "session."}, {"start": 1463.0, "text": "When an NDEF tag is found, it is"}, {"start": 1465.0, "text": "going to be sent to the Delegate"}, {"start": 1467.0, "text": "function."}, {"start": 1468.0, "text": "We connect to the tag and call"}, {"start": 1473.0, "text": "queryNDEFStatus."}, {"start": 1475.0, "text": "If the tag is writeable and has"}, {"start": 1479.0, "text": "sufficient storage, we call the"}, {"start": 1481.0, "text": "writeNDEF function to write to"}, {"start": 1484.0, "text": "the tag."}, {"start": 1486.0, "text": "Finally, we call the"}, {"start": 1487.0, "text": "invalidateFunction to end the"}, {"start": 1488.0, "text": "session."}, {"start": 1492.0, "text": "Now let's take a look how a coupon is created."}, {"start": 1501.0, "text": "Here, we have the createCoupon"}, {"start": 1502.0, "text": "action function."}, {"start": 1505.0, "text": "We instantiate a"}, {"start": 1506.0, "text": "TagReaderSession object."}, {"start": 1509.0, "text": "We call the setAlert message and"}, {"start": 1512.0, "text": "call beginFunction to start a"}, {"start": 1513.0, "text": "session."}, {"start": 1523.0, "text": "Here, we are looking"}, {"start": 1524.0, "text": "specifically for a MIFARE"}, {"start": 1525.0, "text": "Ultralight coupon tag in the"}, {"start": 1527.0, "text": "Delegate function."}, {"start": 1529.0, "text": "When a tag is actually found, we"}, {"start": 1531.0, "text": "connect to it and start the"}, {"start": 1533.0, "text": "write operation."}, {"start": 1542.0, "text": "To write to the tag, we"}, {"start": 1544.0, "text": "basically create a coupon code"}, {"start": 1547.0, "text": "and then call sendMIFARE command"}, {"start": 1549.0, "text": "to start a write operation."}, {"start": 1552.0, "text": "When all write operations are"}, {"start": 1554.0, "text": "completed, we invalidate the"}, {"start": 1557.0, "text": "session."}, {"start": 1562.0, "text": "We have used both NDEF and"}, {"start": 1564.0, "text": "native tag reader session to"}, {"start": 1565.0, "text": "create NFC tags."}, {"start": 1568.0, "text": "Now let's take a look together"}, {"start": 1569.0, "text": "with the Fish Tag Reader app."}, {"start": 1581.0, "text": "The NFCTagReaderSession has"}, {"start": 1583.0, "text": "convenience methods to perform"}, {"start": 1584.0, "text": "NDEF operations."}, {"start": 1587.0, "text": "This is what we use here."}, {"start": 1589.0, "text": "However, it's required us to add"}, {"start": 1591.0, "text": "the 7816 AID and Type F system"}, {"start": 1596.0, "text": "code into the -- for the NDEF in"}, {"start": 1598.0, "text": "our info.plist file, which is"}, {"start": 1600.0, "text": "shown here."}, {"start": 1610.0, "text": "Now in the Scan View controller"}, {"start": 1612.0, "text": "--"}, {"start": 1618.0, "text": "We have the scan tag action"}, {"start": 1621.0, "text": "function."}, {"start": 1622.0, "text": "Here, we create a"}, {"start": 1624.0, "text": "TagReaderSession, set the alert"}, {"start": 1627.0, "text": "message, and call begins to"}, {"start": 1630.0, "text": "start the -- write the Reader"}, {"start": 1632.0, "text": "action function."}, {"start": 1641.0, "text": "When an NFC tag is found, it is"}, {"start": 1643.0, "text": "then delivered to our Delegate"}, {"start": 1644.0, "text": "callback."}, {"start": 1648.0, "text": "We connect to the tag and"}, {"start": 1650.0, "text": "perform NDEF status query."}, {"start": 1655.0, "text": "If the tag is readable, we call"}, {"start": 1657.0, "text": "readNDEF method."}, {"start": 1667.0, "text": "Now let's -- finally, we"}, {"start": 1668.0, "text": "actually invalidate the session"}, {"start": 1669.0, "text": "by calling Invalidate."}, {"start": 1677.0, "text": "Now let's take a look how we"}, {"start": 1678.0, "text": "read a coupon tag."}, {"start": 1687.0, "text": "Here, we have a ScanCoupon"}, {"start": 1688.0, "text": "action function."}, {"start": 1689.0, "text": "And just like before, we"}, {"start": 1691.0, "text": "instantiate a"}, {"start": 1693.0, "text": "NFCTagReaderSession object."}, {"start": 1694.0, "text": "We set the alert message."}, {"start": 1698.0, "text": "And we start a session by"}, {"start": 1699.0, "text": "calling the Begin."}, {"start": 1707.0, "text": "When a tag is found, we check to"}, {"start": 1708.0, "text": "see if it's a MIFARE Ultralight"}, {"start": 1710.0, "text": "tag."}, {"start": 1712.0, "text": "If it is, we connect to the tag."}, {"start": 1723.0, "text": "To read from the tag, we call"}, {"start": 1724.0, "text": "the sendMIFARE command."}, {"start": 1728.0, "text": "We then validate the queue"}, {"start": 1729.0, "text": "point."}, {"start": 1732.0, "text": "At the end, we call the"}, {"start": 1734.0, "text": "Invalidate method to end the"}, {"start": 1736.0, "text": "session."}, {"start": 1740.0, "text": "If the coupon is invalid, we"}, {"start": 1742.0, "text": "call invalidateErrorMessage"}, {"start": 1743.0, "text": "instead."}, {"start": 1749.0, "text": "Now that's everything that you"}, {"start": 1750.0, "text": "need in order to create a great"}, {"start": 1752.0, "text": "app using the Core NFC"}, {"start": 1754.0, "text": "Framework. Back to Gordon."}, {"start": 1764.0, "text": "Thank you, Lawrence."}, {"start": 1768.0, "text": "So we hope the new tag writing"}, {"start": 1769.0, "text": "and native access allows you to"}, {"start": 1771.0, "text": "add awesome new features to your"}, {"start": 1772.0, "text": "applications."}, {"start": 1773.0, "text": "As we've seen, it's pretty"}, {"start": 1774.0, "text": "straightforward and pretty"}, {"start": 1775.0, "text": "simple."}, {"start": 1776.0, "text": "Let's do a quick review of what"}, {"start": 1777.0, "text": "we've gone over today."}, {"start": 1779.0, "text": "First, decide which type of"}, {"start": 1781.0, "text": "reader session your application"}, {"start": 1782.0, "text": "has required."}, {"start": 1783.0, "text": "NDEF, native access, or even"}, {"start": 1784.0, "text": "both."}, {"start": 1789.0, "text": "Implement the newDelegate methods to receive the new tag"}, {"start": 1790.0, "text": "objects."}, {"start": 1793.0, "text": "Once you have those tag objects,"}, {"start": 1794.0, "text": "go ahead and perform all your"}, {"start": 1796.0, "text": "reads and writes using those objects."}, {"start": 1799.0, "text": "And when you're all done,"}, {"start": 1800.0, "text": "indicate the proper success or"}, {"start": 1801.0, "text": "error indication using the"}, {"start": 1802.0, "text": "appropriate Invalidation call."}, {"start": 1806.0, "text": "And that's it."}, {"start": 1810.0, "text": "So all the sample code that we"}, {"start": 1811.0, "text": "have gone through today is"}, {"start": 1812.0, "text": "available to you online now,"}, {"start": 1814.0, "text": "along with other information."}, {"start": 1816.0, "text": "iOS 13 is available now along"}, {"start": 1818.0, "text": "with Xcode 11."}, {"start": 1819.0, "text": "Everybody should go ahead"}, {"start": 1820.0, "text": "download that and use Core NFC"}, {"start": 1822.0, "text": "to start doing awesome, new"}, {"start": 1823.0, "text": "things."}, {"start": 1825.0, "text": "And if anybody has questions,"}, {"start": 1826.0, "text": "the Core NFC Lab is immediately"}, {"start": 1827.0, "text": "following this session over in"}, {"start": 1829.0, "text": "the labs. So come talk to us and say"}, {"start": 1831.0, "text": "hello."}]}
